fastest_sites walks every MASTER_SITE_* mirror list defined in
Mk/bsd.sites.mk and measures the TCP handshake latency to each mirror,
then prints the list sorted from fastest to slowest. The output is
suitable for redirecting into a file (e.g. /usr/local/etc/ports_sites.conf)
and including from /etc/make.conf, so the ports build system prefers the
nearest/fastest mirrors when fetching distfiles.

This is a locally reconstructed port: the official ports-mgmt/fastest_sites
was removed from the FreeBSD ports tree on 2019-10-16 (unmaintained,
unfetchable). This variant is a Python 3 port of the original author's
script (originally Python 2 only, using the `asyncore` module which was
removed in Python 3.12). The connection-timing logic has been rewritten
using non-blocking sockets and select() instead.

WWW: https://github.com/jordansissel/fastest_sites
